摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DSH plugin · Drive the local Moli headless browser from DeepSeek Harness: moli_fetch and moli_probe for JS-rendered pages, Markdown, semantic trees, screenshots and PDFs, with sandbox-aware failure classification.","id":"gh:1415767842","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-moli","slug":"27painter/dsh-moli","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","headless-browser","markdown","moli","screenshot","windows"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DSH plugin · Drive the local Moli headless browser from DeepSeek Harness: moli_fetch and moli_probe "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"for JS-rendered pages, Markdown, semantic trees, screenshots and PDFs, with sandbox-aware failure cl"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"ed pages, Markdown, semantic trees, screenshots and PDFs, with sandbox-aware failure classification."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-moli"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Two tools that let a DeepSeek Harness agent drive a real headless browser.** They wrap\nMoli — a Ru"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"st headless browser built for AI agents — so an agent can\nread pages that only exist after JavaScrip"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"t runs, and can produce pictures of them."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## What it does, and when you want it"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"A plain HTTP fetch returns the HTML the server sent. That is enough for articles, docs and APIs, and"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"\nDSH already covers it with `web_fetch`. It is not enough for anything a browser has to build:"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- **Single-page apps** — a client-rendered news site, dashboard or docs site. The response is an emp"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"ty\nshell; the content appears only after scripts run.\n- **Logins and consent walls** — a page that n"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"eeds a session or cookie before it shows anything.\n- **Pictures** — a screenshot to see what a page "},{"id":"p7s4","text":"looks like, or a PDF to keep.\n- **One value from deep inside a page** — a price, a count, a title, r"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"ead with a selector instead of\npulling the whole document.\n- **A list you can read for 7% of the pag"},{"id":"p7s6","text":"e** — `selector` returns only the matched containers, which\non a real feed measured 1,779 characters"},{"id":"p7s7","text":" against 139,338 for the same page as Markdown. If you are\nabout to fetch a listing page and skim it"},{"id":"p7s8","text":", read the `selector` section under Usage first."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"For those jobs this plugin gives the agent two tools:"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| Tool | What it does |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| `moli_fetch` | Renders a URL and returns Markdown, HTML, a semantic tree, or a JSON envelope carry"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"ing the HTTP status; **reads one container with `selector`**; evaluates a JavaScript expression; wri"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"tes a PNG screenshot or a PDF |\n| `moli_probe` | Reports whether the engine is installed, which vers"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"ion, and whether HTTPS works — and installs Moli when it is missing |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"The practical question is whether the agent needs the page as a **browser** would see it. If a plain"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"\nfetch already returns the text you want, `web_fetch` is lighter and faster."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### `scroll` — reach what only appears on a scroll"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"The engine serializes the whole document, so a plain fetch already contains everything the DOM holds"},{"id":"p14s2","text":" serializes the whole document, so a plain fetch already contains everything the DOM holds.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Known limitations"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"- **The Linux and macOS paths were written, and the maintainer's own hardware cannot run them.** The"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"\nmaintainer is a student with no macOS or Linux machine, so engine discovery at the POSIX locations\n"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"and the `sh` installer route came from @nd002723. Linux was verified\nby them on Ubuntu 24.04; macOS "},{"id":"p16s4","text":"is now covered by CI, which installs the official darwin build and\nruns the page-level suites on `ma"},{"id":"p16s5","text":"cos-latest` (Apple Silicon, arm64) — see\nPlatform support for exactly what that exercised. **A CI ru"},{"id":"p16s6","text":"nner is not a\ndesktop, so if something fails on either platform, please open an\nissue with the error"},{"id":"p16s7","text":" output** — that is still the\nonly way the paths users actually take get fixed.\n- **Moli itself is n"},{"id":"p16s8","text":"ot bundled.** Install it separately or let `moli_probe action=install` fetch it.\n- **Only `fetch` is"},{"id":"p16s9","text":" wrapped.** `moli serve` (CDP/WebDriver server) and `moli import` (session\nimport) are not exposed a"},{"id":"p16s10","text":"s tools yet.\n- **No per-call cancellation for fetches.** The engine runs synchronously for a fetch, "},{"id":"p16s11","text":"so an\ninterrupted turn cannot abort it mid-flight; a call already in progress finishes and its artif"},{"id":"p16s12","text":"act\nis written. `moli_probe action=install` is the exception — it is asynchronous and aborts the chi"},{"id":"p16s13","text":"ld\nimmediately on an interrupted turn.\n- **HTTP error status is only visible for `dump: json`.** Tha"},{"id":"p16s14","text":"t is the only dump format carrying the\nstatus field. With `markdown` or `html` an error page is retu"},{"id":"p16s15","text":"rned as content.\n- **`writeTo` calls are serialized.** They report as unsafe to parallelize, so two "},{"id":"p16s16","text":"artifact writes\nnever interleave.\n- **`insecureTls` defaults to `true`.** Behind a filtering proxy t"},{"id":"p16s17","text":"he certificate-revocation\nresponder is often unreachable, and Schannel then fails with\n`CRYPT_E_REVO"},{"id":"p16s18","text":"CATION_OFFLINE (0x80092013)` on hosts like GitHub. The default passes moli's\n`--insecure-disable-tls"},{"id":"p16s19","text":"-host-verification`. Set `insecureTls: false` on networks where revocation\nchecks work, or per call "},{"id":"p16s20","text":"with `insecureTls: false`.\n- **Sandbox interaction.** Under DSH's default file sandbox, a subprocess"},{"id":"p16s21","text":" runs at low integrity and\nSchannel cannot acquire client credentials, so HTTPS fails with `SEC_E_NO"},{"id":"p16s22","text":"_CREDENTIALS`. Plain\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"### Prerequisites for the suites"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"The plugin has one optional runtime dependency — `@deepseek-ai/schemastery` — used by the live `Conf"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"ig` schema that registers the settings namespace (optional because the import is guarded, so a `link"},{"id":"p18s3","text":":` install without it still loads and registers the tools). Suites that import the plugin (`config-v"},{"id":"p18s4","text":"erify`, `schema-verify`, `empty-verify`, `report-verify`, `http-verify`) need it resolvable from the"},{"id":"p18s5","text":" working tree, so run `npm install` first."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"`schema-verify` additionally imports the registry's own validator out of the npm-global `@deepseek-a"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"i/dsh` install (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools`); `report-verify` and the engine suites need a real Moli en"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"gine, and `empty-verify` needs a C compiler to build its stub engines. On Windows, `@deepseek-ai/sch"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"emastery` can be resolved through a directory junction into the fork's `node_modules` from the npm-g"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"lobal DSH tree, the same way the suites resolve `dsh-tools`."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Beyond those, `lib/moli.js` and the tool layer were exercised end to end against Moli 1.1.16 on\nWind"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ows: registration, probe, Markdown and JSON dumps, `eval` (including a tight-timeout regression\nguar"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"d for the `-t` argument position), PNG and PDF artifacts with valid signatures, truncation, every\nre"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"jection path (binary dump without `writeTo`, unknown `dump`, unknown `wait` stage, missing\ndestinati"},{"id":"p20s5","text":"on directory), failure classification (unreachable host, HTTP status, sandbox TLS block,\nrevocation "},{"id":"p20s6","text":"block), and the concurrency claims. The blocked-host classifier is covered by pure\nfunction tests us"},{"id":"p20s7","text":"ing stderr text captured from real runs."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Confirmed at runtime too: a JavaScript-rendered page (GitHub search) returned 14,560 characters of\nM"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"arkdown containing 30 real repository matches when fetched through a local proxy. A throwaway\nprofil"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"e with the plugin installed composes its config with no `JsonSchemaError` and no skipped bundle."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
